4579,3,151645,198,151644,77091,198],"messages":[{"content":"Solve the problem step by step. Give your final answer in \\boxed{...}.\n\nLet  \\[ f(x) =\n\\begin{cases}\n-\\sqrt[3]x & \\text{if } x \\geq 0,\\\\\nx^2& \\text{if } x <0.\n\\end{cases}\n\\]Compute $f(f(f(f(512)))).$","role":"user"}],"rendered_sha256":"6eaa74fc852308ea39fdc263c712093bf7e3b0e90046beba8860247f0b0ec5b6"},"seconds":12.464045286178589,"seed":405559602253090195,"stop":"eos","text":"To solve \\( f(f(f(f(512)))) \\), we need to evaluate the function \\( f \\) step by step. Let's start with the innermost function and work our way out.\n\n1. **First evaluation: \\( f(512) \\)**\n\n   Given \\( 512 \\geq 0 \\), we use the first case of the piecewise function:\n   \\[\n   f(512) = -\\sqrt[3]{512}\n   \\]\n   Calculate the cube root of 512:\n   \\[\n   \\sqrt[3]{512} = 8\n   \\]\n   Therefore,\n   \\[\n   f(512) = -8\n   \\]\n\n2. **Second evaluation: \\( f(f(512)) = f(-8) \\)**\n\n   Given \\( -8 < 0 \\), we use the second case of the piecewise function:\n   \\[\n   f(-8) = (-8)^2\n   \\]\n   Calculate the square of -8:\n   \\[\n   (-8)^2 = 64\n   \\]\n   Therefore,\n   \\[\n   f(-8) = 64\n   \\]\n\n3. **Third evaluation: \\( f(f(f(512))) = f(64) \\)**\n\n   Given \\( 64 \\geq 0 \\), we use the first case of the piecewise function:\n   \\[\n   f(64) = -\\sqrt[3]{64}\n   \\]\n   Calculate the cube root of 64:\n   \\[\n   \\sqrt[3]{64} = 4\n   \\]\n   Therefore,\n   \\[\n   f(64) = -4\n   \\]\n\n4. **Fourth evaluation: \\( f(f(f(f(512)))) = f(-4) \\)**\n\n   Given \\( -4 < 0 \\), we use the second case of the piecewise function:\n   \\[\n   f(-4) = (-4)^2\n   \\]\n   Calculate the square of -4:\n   \\[\n   (-4)^2 = 16\n   \\]\n   Therefore,\n   \\[\n   f(-4) = 16\n   \\]\n\nThus, the final answer is:\n\\[\n\\boxed{16}\n\\]"},"grade":{"answer":"\\boxed{16}","correct":true,"format":"boxed","parseable":true},"id":"algebra:273"}
